# React security

## XSS

- Default: render user text as `{value}` — never unsanitized HTML
- `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` only with DOMPurify at the same call site — flag in review

## URLs

Validate `href`/`src` schemes — allow `http:`, `https:`, `mailto:` only for user-provided links.

## External links

```tsx
<a href={url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
```

## Env vars (Vite)

Only `VITE_*` vars are public in the client bundle. Never prefix secrets with `VITE_`.

## Auth UI

Hiding UI is not authorization. RLS and server checks must enforce access.

## Session storage

Do not store session tokens in `localStorage`. Follow Supabase auth patterns already in the app.
